course: dictionary
lesson: 10054
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word test has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. As a noun, a test can be a set of questions that checks what you know, as in «take a test» or «pass a test». It can also be a check to find out if something works or is true, like an eye test.
explain: As a verb, to test means to check or try something to find out about it. Scientists test an idea with an experiment, and doctors test eyes and hearing. When you meet test, ask yourself: is someone checking what I know, or checking whether something works?
explain: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board, so his teacher sends him for an eye test.» The clue is eye: the test checks whether his eyes work. Swap in your meaning, "a check to find out if something works", and the sentence still makes sense. That is how you know you have it right.
fact: As a noun, test can mean a set of questions that checks what you know.
fact: As a noun, test can also mean a check to find out if something works or is true.
fact: As a verb, «test» means to check or try something to find out about it.
fact: In a fair test you change only one thing and keep everything else the same, so you know what caused any change.
fact: Before a new medicine is sold, it is tested on many volunteers and compared with a dummy pill to make sure it really works and is safe.
exercise: Ruby says, «I have a spelling test on Friday.» What is a test here? | *A set of questions that checks what you know | A loud noise | A kind of sweet | A long walk in the hills
exercise: «Scientists test the idea with an experiment.» What does test mean here? | *To check or try something to find out about it | To forget something | To sing a song loudly | To wrap something up carefully
exercise: «In a fair test you change only one thing.» Which word is the noun in this sentence? | *test | keep | change | only
test: «Pass» in «pass a test» means what? | *To do well enough on a check | To hand something to someone | To fail to answer | To leave the room quietly
test: Which sentence uses test as a verb? | A spelling test is on Friday. | Mum took me for an eye test. | The test was long and hard. | *Doctors test children's hearing every year.
exam: In «A boy in Halifax has an eye test», what does test mean? | *A check to find out if something works or is true | Chance to try a new sport | A kind of game | A type of glasses | A set of school questions
